From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000003 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ReForge <reforge@flashforge>
Date: Fri, 05 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gcode: use a raw string for the m112 regex

The non-raw m112 regex contains an unrecognized Python string escape.
Python 3.6–3.11 emits a usually hidden DeprecationWarning; 3.12–3.14 emits
SyntaxWarning. A future SyntaxError transition has no release specified in
Python 3.14's lexical reference. It is not a Python 3.14 import blocker.

A raw string removes the warning without changing the regex. See
https://docs.python.org/3.14/reference/lexical_analysis.html#unrecognized-escape-sequences
and docs/research/2026-06-04-klipper-v0.11-fork-deltas.md for the correction.

Signed-off-by: ReForge <reforge@flashforge>
---
 klippy/gcode.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/klippy/gcode.py b/klippy/gcode.py
--- a/klippy/gcode.py
+++ b/klippy/gcode.py
@@ -393,7 +393,7 @@ class GCodeIO:
         self._dump_debug()
         if self.is_fileinput:
             self.printer.request_exit('error_exit')
-    m112_r = re.compile('^(?:[nN][0-9]+)?\s*[mM]112(?:\s|$)')
+    m112_r = re.compile(r'^(?:[nN][0-9]+)?\s*[mM]112(?:\s|$)')
     def _process_data(self, eventtime):
         # Read input, separate by newline, and add to pending_commands
         try:
